; The program writes an @external var each frame; the embedder reads it
; after each frame boundary: each frame's write is published at the frame
; boundary for the embedder's next read to adopt. (@external vars can't
; have initializers — storage starts zeroed, and seeding is the embedder's
; job through the handle.)
@external
(var level: f32)

@cpu
(defn main []
  (spawn-window (fn []
                    (= level (+ level 0.25)))))
